---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro';
import Code from '../../../components/docs/Code.astro';
import DeviceConstraints from '../../../components/docs/DeviceConstraints.astro';
import { page } from '../../../data/docs-nav';

const entry = page('/docs/destinations/folder/');

const names = `hozz-20260822T211046Z-2f1a9c04-000000.ndjson
hozz-20260822T211046Z-2f1a9c04-000001.ndjson
hozz-20260822T221512Z-2f1a9c04-000002.ndjson`;
---

<DocsLayout page={entry} section="Destinations">
  <div class="fact-strip">
    <div>
      <dt>Format</dt>
      <dd>NDJSON, JSON, CSV or Metrics JSON</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Needs</dt>
      <dd>Nothing but the Files app</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Recommended</dt>
      <dd>Yes — start here</dd>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Hozz writes batches to any folder in Files: cloud storage, SMB or on-device.
  </p>

  <p>
    Cloud-backed and on-device folders need no server, open port or VPN. SMB requires its host
    to remain reachable.
  </p>

  <h2>Setting it up</h2>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h3>Choose a folder</h3>
      <p>
        Anywhere Files can reach.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Let the folder sync</h3>
      <p>Hozz writes files; your provider moves them.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Send a test</h3>
      <p>A probe file appears in the folder. If you can see it, the destination works.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What lands in the folder</h2>

  <p>Files are named so they sort chronologically and cannot collide:</p>

  <Code caption="hozz-&lt;timestamp&gt;-&lt;destination&gt;-&lt;sequence&gt;.&lt;ext&gt;" code={names} />

  <p>
    The timestamp, destination id and sequence keep names ordered and unique.
  </p>

  <p>
    Pick the format on the destination:{' '}
    <a href="/docs/delivery-schema/#ndjson">NDJSON</a> (the default, and lossless),{' '}
    <a href="/docs/delivery-schema/#json">JSON</a>,{' '}
    <a href="/docs/delivery-schema/#csv">CSV</a>, or{' '}
    <a href="/docs/delivery-schema/#metrics-json">Metrics JSON</a>.
  </p>

  <Callout kind="warn" title="Line protocol is not offered for folders">
    <p>
      The Mac watcher ignores line protocol, so Hozz does not offer that combination.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Pairing it with the Mac app</h2>

  <p>
    Point the phone and <a href="/docs/destinations/mac/">Mac app</a> at the same synced folder to
    get charts and <a href="/docs/mcp/">assistant access</a> without inbound connections.
  </p>

  <h2>When it goes wrong</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong><em>Hozz could not reach that folder. It may have been moved, renamed, or signed
          out.</em></strong>
      Pick the folder again.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><em>Hozz no longer has permission to write to that folder.</em></strong>
      Pick it again to restore access.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    The cursor advances only after a successful write, so neither failure loses records.
  </p>

  <DeviceConstraints />
</DocsLayout>
